<title>BELGIUM: EU to extend French buckwheat planting deadline.</title>
<headline>EU to extend French buckwheat planting deadline.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is likely to propose an extension of the area aid planting deadline for French buckwheat by two weeks until the end of May, an EU member state official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official, speaking after a meeting of EU grain experts last week, said France requested the extension, which would apply to less than 1,000 hectares in Brittany, because wet conditions delayed planting.</p>
<p>Sweden also wants to extend the planting deadline for three Swedish counties by two weeks until mid-June due to long winters.</p>
<p>Separately, Greece requested an increase of 19,764 hectares in its irrigated cereals and oilseed area eligible for EU aid. The increase would cover irrigation projects started, but not completed before August 1992.</p>
<p>The European Commission asked Greece to propose changes to its regional cereals and oilseed area aid programmes to ensure that the overall historic yield, upon which EU subsidy payments are based, remained unchanged.</p>
<p>-Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
